  "lineage": "Onmyōdō ('the way of yin and yang') was the Japanese esoteric cosmological practice of the Heian-period court, institutionalized in the Onmyōryō bureau and epitomized by the tenth-century master Abe no Seimei, blending Chinese yin-yang and Five-Phase theory with Daoist, Shinto, and Buddhist elements. Its ritual voice includes spells (ju), the recitation of formulae, and protective incantations accompanying divination, exorcism, and star-worship (such as rites to the Northern Dipper). Delivery is a measured, metrically-bound intonation of classical Chinese and Japanese formulae, learned through hereditary specialist lineages (the Abe/Tsuchimikado and Kamo houses). The tradition is documented in Heian court records and ritual manuals and persists in attenuated folk and reconstructed forms.",
